* MiCA Titles VI–VII\nMarket abuse and enforcement
** Scope of Title VI (Art. 86)
*** Crypto-assets admitted (or requested) to trading
*** Any person, on or off platform
*** In the Union and in third countries
** Inside information (Arts 87–88)
*** Precise, non-public, price-sensitive
*** Disclosure as soon as possible, 5-year archive
*** Delay: legitimate interest, not misleading, confidential
*** ESAP filing from 10 January 2030 (Art. 110a)
** Prohibitions (Arts 89–91)
*** Insider dealing, incl. cancelling orders
*** Insiders include DLT roles: validators, developers
*** Unlawful disclosure
*** Manipulation: false signals, artificial price, deception
*** Spoofing, layering, cornering, undisclosed promotion
** Detection (Art. 92)
*** Intermediaries: systems to prevent and detect
*** Report suspicions, incl. consensus anomalies
** National authorities (Arts 93–102)
*** Powers: information, suspension 30 days, prohibition
*** Inspections, freezing, content removal
*** Cooperation, classification convergence
*** Precautionary measures by host authorities
** Product intervention (Arts 103–105)
*** ESMA: other crypto-assets
*** EBA: ARTs and EMTs
*** National authorities
** ESMA registers (Arts 109–110)
*** White papers, issuers, CASPs
*** Non-compliant entities
** Penalties (Arts 111–116)
*** Natural persons ≥ EUR 700 000
*** Legal persons ≥ EUR 5 M or 3 / 5 / 12.5 % turnover
*** Market abuse: ≥ EUR 5 M / EUR 15 M or 15 %, 3× profit
*** Management bans, publication, whistleblowers
** EBA supervision (Arts 117–138)
*** Significant ART and EMT issuers
*** Crypto-asset committee, supervisory colleges
*** Investigations, on-site inspections
*** Fines up to 12.5 % / 10 % turnover
*** Periodic penalties 3 % daily turnover
*** Court of Justice review, fees, delegation
